  "lines": 316,
  "scope": "One actual original-edge-list program performs sorting, seed filtering and draw-record construction, then hands those literal returned records to the actual matrix/forest/candidate interpreter. Original-only size/sum bounds cover the full trace. The original finite assignment-law endpoint now consumes the unsorted original graph edge enumeration and canonical original weight/draw records; same seed/forest choices and corrected stretch/lightness/failure constants. Seed/forest/random generation, raw representation and physical bit cost remain explicit."
